.Dd November 25, 2026
.Dt HMKTST 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm hmktst
.Nd run the usual storage and disk-count auction searches
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm hmktst
.Op Ar hcli-flags ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a
.Xr sh 1
wrapper.
It calls
.Pa ~/bin/hcli
five times with
.Fl p Cm market
and prints a label before each table.
.Ev HCLI
overrides that path.
Extra arguments are appended to every call.
Each call uses the cached auction list when it is still fresh.
.Pp
Each search passes one
.Fl o
starting with
.Cm format=price,re=ECC,re=ENT
and the extra pairs below.
Both patterns must match.
.Pp
A row needs ECC and ENT in the disk, CPU, or description text.
.Pp
The five searches, in order:
.Bl -tag -width "Storage min 40g price max 100" -compact
.It Storage min 40g price max 100
.Cm disk.min=40000
and
.Cm price.max=100
.It Storage min 27g price max 80
.Cm disk.min=27000
and
.Cm price.max=80
.It Disk count min 5 price max 80
.Cm disk.count.min=5
and
.Cm price.max=80
.It Lotta disk cheap
.Cm disk.min=80000
.It Lucky draw: 7 disk min
.Cm disk.count.min=7
.El
.Pp
.Cm disk.min
is total gigabytes, count times size.
40000 is 40 TB in the old decimal unit.
The prices in the labels are euros.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The exit status is the status of the last
.Xr hcli 1
call.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr hcli 1 ,
.Xr hmktvm 1 ,
.Xr hmktvm-picky 1
